<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - MGX SIXTEEN-MO SHARE RISES.</title>
<headline>TABLE - MGX SIXTEEN-MO SHARE RISES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sixteen months to June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		 47.7	 vs  24.7</p>
<p>    - attrib		   46.0	 vs  30.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    13.28	vs   7.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    19.10	vs  11.35</p>
<p>    Tax			   6.53	vs   3.53</p>
<p>    Interest received	 0.53	vs   0.14</p>
<p>    Turnover		  120.40	vs  45.03</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	    0.5 loss  vs   1.39 profit</p>
<p>Full name: MGX Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would award capitalisation shares of 0.6146 cents each to shareholders registered on August 29. The shares would be awarded in the ratio of 0.96 new shares for every 100 held.</p>
<p>It said that in the absence of unforseen circumstances, it epxected to continue to grow its earnings per share at above average rates and to generate positive cash flows.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
